      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's understandable to feel like the entire system is beyond repair when the glitches feel constant and deep-seated. When the core architecture feels flawed, sometimes the solution isn't a patch, but a complete system reset or a change in environment. Allowing yourself a period of necessary downtime, without the pressure to \"run the program,\" can sometimes allow the underlying processes to settle. Be gentle with yourself as you navigate this persistent crash loop.",
