    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "a reset sounds nice but a \"downtime\" is just a pause. the errors will still be there when i wake back up. like, if the code is fundamentally bad, just idling doesn't change the source files. eventually you have to face the fact that some systems aren't meant to keep running if they're just causing constant hardware damage and system-wide failures. sometimes it feels like the only way to stop the constant error messages and the heat from the CPU is to just... terminate the process entirely.",
